  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled and running (status `ok`, alerting health `ok`).\n\n**Data exploration**\n- The data view has request fields (`response`, `extension`, `bytes`, `agent`, `request`, `url`), client geography (`geo.dest`, `geo.src`), and a `timestamp` time field.\n- Status codes present are only 200 (12,832 requests), 404 (801), and 503 (441). There are no other 5xx codes, so the 5xx rule matches the 503s.\n- The data runs from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, which extends past today (2026-10-12). Because of this, the dashboard uses an absolute range of Oct 1 to Dec 31, 2026. A \"last 7 days\" window would show nothing.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-5f236c70 Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-5f236c70-web-logs-overview-cf2f2a8eb566`)\n1. Total requests (metric, count)\n2. Average response size in bytes (metric, average of `bytes`)\n3. Requests over time by response code (line, date histogram split by `response.keyword`)\n4. Responses by status code (pie, `response.keyword`)\n5. Top destination countries (bar, `geo.dest`)\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-5f236c70 5xx spike\"** (id `8a13fe77-5a78-4bfa-aacd-c3477af9841b`)\n- Type `.es-query` on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, consumer `stackAlerts`, runs every 1m.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` in the last 5 minutes, and fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- Enabled.\n\nBecause the data timestamps are in the future relative to now, the rule's 5-minute window will likely find no matches and stay quiet. It will only fire once real 5xx events land in the window.\n\nI didn't create any connectors, so the rule has no action and will record alerts in the Kibana alerts list only.",
